---
import InfoLayout from '../../layouts/InfoLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
---

<InfoLayout
  title="About Infinite Calculators"
  description="Who runs Infinite Calculators, why the site exists, how each calculator is checked before it goes live, and how the site is paid for. Free, no sign-up."
  h1="About Infinite Calculators"
>
  <p>
    Infinite Calculators publishes free calculators for everyday questions: how many hours are on a time
    card, how much concrete a slab needs, what to tip, what score you need on a final exam, how much zakat
    is due, and when Easter falls in a given year.
  </p>

  <h2>Why this site exists</h2>
  <p>
    Many calculator sites give you a number without showing how they got it. We build every calculator
    to the same four rules:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>It gives the answer as you type, on a phone as well as a computer.</li>
    <li>It explains the formula in plain language, with a worked example you can check by hand.</li>
    <li>It runs entirely in your browser, so the numbers you enter are never sent to us.</li>
    <li>It is free to use, with no account or sign-up.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we check our calculators</h2>
  <p>
    The math behind each calculator is written as a small, separate piece of code and tested against
    known answers before the page goes live. Depending on the calculator, those answers come from
    published dates, official rate tables or examples worked out by hand.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where the answer depends on a choice of method, the page says which method it uses. For example, the
    zakat calculator lets you choose between the gold and silver nisab, and the Hijri date converter
    explains that local moon sighting can move a date by a day.
  </p>

  <h2>Who runs the site</h2>
  {/* TODO(owner): replace this paragraph with a short, real description of who runs the site. */}
  <p>
    Infinite Calculators is an independent website. It is not owned by, or affiliated with, any bank,
    retailer, school or religious organization.
  </p>

  <h2>How the site is paid for</h2>
  <p>
    The site is free to use. Its running costs are covered by advertising shown through Google AdSense.
    Advertisers have no say in how any calculator works or what it tells you. Our
    <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a> explains how ads and cookies work on this site.
  </p>

  <h2>Found a mistake?</h2>
  <p>
    If a result looks wrong, please <a href="/contact/">tell us</a> or email
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. Include the page, the numbers you entered and the
    answer you expected, and we will check it.
  </p>
</InfoLayout>
